- [LOUD CRASH]

21
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:41,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

22
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,867
<i>Sam needs a father
who will guide her.</i>

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,667
<i> She needs you desperately.</i>

24
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:51,833
<i>You violated
your agency's protocol?</i>

25
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:53,400
<i> We caught Mr. Chan.</i>

26
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:55,367
<i>We're so close
to solving this case.</i>

27
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:58,033
<i>You know how much the name
you bear means to me.</i>

28
00:01:58,167 --> 00:01:59,700
I will give you one more chance.

29
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:01,267
<i>The moment you tarnish
my name,</i>

30
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,133
I'll disown you as my daughter.

31
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,033
You've waited so long for this.

32
00:02:07,167 --> 00:02:09,767
<i>He took advantage
and belittled me.</i>

33
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:12,767
<i>The day will come where
the tables will turn.</i>

34
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,900
<i> Gabo, tell me the truth.</i>

35
00:02:15,067 --> 00:02:16,700
<i> I took on a sideline.</i>

36
00:02:16,833 --> 00:02:19,533
<i>I got some gold, Pa.
When I got it,</i>

37
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:23,167
<i>I got second thoughts about
whether I should return it.</i>

38
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,500
<i> I felt guilty.</i>

39
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:26,367
<i> I chose to do the right thing.</i>

40
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:29,700
<i>I'm so proud of you, Gabo.
You've made me so happy.</i>

41
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,000
I feel sorry for you, Gabo.

42
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:40,100
You shouldn't have to experience
a life like this.

43
00:02:40,233 --> 00:02:46,267
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,667
Do you still remember...

45
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:50,700
when you were a child,

46
00:02:51,933 --> 00:02:53,633
our life was luxurious?

47
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,300
But...

48
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:58,700
It all disappeared.

49
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:05,400
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

50
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:07,000
I remember, Pa.

51
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:10,700
I remembered everything.

52
00:03:12,267 --> 00:03:13,600
[SIGHS]

53
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,800
A Japanese man
once asked

54
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:22,800
for my help to look
for a treasure.

55
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:29,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

56
00:03:32,367 --> 00:03:33,300
<i> Nice!</i>

57
00:03:37,067 --> 00:03:39,000
<i> Sir! Good evening!</i>

58
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:41,567
<i>- Sorry to keep you waiting.
- It's alright, sir.</i>

59
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,133
<i> Don't worry. Be happy.</i>

60
00:03:43,267 --> 00:03:45,000
<i> That's why you're my favorite.</i>

61
00:03:45,567 --> 00:03:46,700
<i>- Let's go, sir.
- Let's go.</i>

62
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:47,800
[ENGINE HUMMS]

63
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:51,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

64
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:52,900
[TIRES SCREECH]

65
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:53,933
<i> Get in!</i>

66
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,267
[GRUNTS]

67
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,767
<i>- Give me your wallet!
- What are you doing?</i>

68
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,933
- [SCREAMING]
- [BONES CRUNCHING]

69
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,300
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GRUNTS]

70
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,633
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [GROANS]

71
00:04:04,767 --> 00:04:06,100
[GROANS]

72
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:11,200
- [GRUNTS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

73
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:14,200
[POLICE SIREN BLARING]

74
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:15,900
- [GRUNTS]
- [KNIFE SWISHES]

75
00:04:16,033 --> 00:04:17,100
[GROANS]

76
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:19,667
[POLICE SIREN BLARING]

77
00:04:20,733 --> 00:04:22,367
- [GRUNTS]
- [BLOW LANDS]

78
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:24,367
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

79
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:26,567
- [GROANS]
- Put your hands up!

80
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:27,967
<i>- Sir...
- Get down!</i>

81
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:29,500
[YOUNG RICARDO] Put
your hands up!

82
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:34,867
<i> Sir Tanaka!</i>

83
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:37,600
<i> Treasure...</i>

84
00:04:37,733 --> 00:04:39,267
<i> G-Gold...</i>

85
00:04:43,267 --> 00:04:44,233
<i> Sir!</i>

86
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:51,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

87
00:04:56,767 --> 00:04:59,200
<i> What are you doing here, Rudy?</i>

88
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:01,033
<i>Thank goodness
we were doing our rounds.</i>

89
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,567
<i> You could've gotten hurt.</i>

90
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:05,167
[YOUNG RICARDO] What's that?

91
00:05:06,133 --> 00:05:07,067
<i> Sir.</i>

92
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,500
<i> A treasure map.</i>

93
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:16,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

94
00:05:21,567 --> 00:05:24,500
<i>I've been working for Tanaka
for a few months, sir.</i>

95
00:05:24,633 --> 00:05:28,100
<i>That's why I know about the
treasure they're looking for.</i>

96
00:05:28,233 --> 00:05:31,367
<i>We heard that there are
a lot of Japanese people here.</i>

97
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:34,633
<i>But how do we know that
that map is real?</i>

98
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:37,000
<i> Tanaka's father was a soldier.</i>

99
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:38,300
<i> He had a lot of meetings.</i>

100
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:40,067
<i> From what I've heard,</i>

101
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:44,467
<i>there's a ton
of gold and jewelry.</i>

102
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:48,200
<i>He's looking for statues
made of gold, sir.</i>

103
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:51,400
<i>The newspaper said that there
were businessmen, politicians,</i>

104
00:05:51,533 --> 00:05:55,533
<i>and treasure hunters silently
digging up in provinces.</i>

105
00:05:55,667 --> 00:05:58,867
<i> And they all come back rich!</i>

106
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,333
<i>In fact, there's a group
that's looking for it in here.</i>

107
00:06:03,267 --> 00:06:06,500
<i> But now that Tanaka is gone...</i>

108
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:10,400
<i>no one will fund
the search anymore.</i>

109
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:13,433
<i>If it were me,
I'd invest in this.</i>

110
00:06:13,567 --> 00:06:15,867
<i> This is an absolute jackpot!</i>

111
00:06:16,533 --> 00:06:18,000
<i> But the problem is...</i>

112
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,033
<i>I don't have
the budget for it.</i>

113
00:06:29,333 --> 00:06:30,333
<i> What do you need</i>

114
00:06:31,833 --> 00:06:33,333
<i> for you to find this treasure?</i>

115
00:06:33,467 --> 00:06:34,900
[YOUNG MARIANO] Oh no, sir...

116
00:06:35,033 --> 00:06:36,500
<i>you'll need
a lot of money for that.</i>

117
00:06:36,633 --> 00:06:39,167
<i>You'll pay for the people,
food--</i>

118
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,067
[YOUNG RUDY] Sir,
if we get lucky,

119
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:42,933
<i>we could get a million
in return.</i>

120
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:44,267
It could come back double, sir.

121
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,833
<i>This chance comes
once in a lifetime.</i>

122
00:06:46,967 --> 00:06:48,533
<i> This comes once in a lifetime.</i>

123
00:06:50,667 --> 00:06:53,233
<i> Fine. I'll finance it.</i>

124
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:57,467
<i>But when we find
this treasure,</i>

125
00:06:58,733 --> 00:06:59,867
<i> we'll have to split it.</i>

126
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,000
<i> Sixty.</i>

127
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,800
<i> Forty.</i>

128
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,767
<i>I can trust you,
right, Rudy?</i>

129
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,733
<i>As if I wasn't
your former asset, sir.</i>

130
00:07:09,867 --> 00:07:10,767
<i> Sir, cheers.</i>

131
00:07:11,267 --> 00:07:12,400
<i>- Cheers.
- Cheers.</i>

132
00:07:12,533 --> 00:07:15,733
[HOST]<i> And now, the moment
</i> everyone is waiting for,

133
00:07:16,133 --> 00:07:18,167
<i> the Golden Star of the night,</i>

134
00:07:18,300 --> 00:07:20,167
<i> Belinda!</i>

135
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:27,267
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:07:35,267 --> 00:07:37,567
[RUDY] When I first saw
your mother,

137
00:07:38,533 --> 00:07:40,533
<i> I was enchanted by her beauty.</i>

138
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,833
<i> And I told myself that</i>

139
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:50,333
<i> I would marry this woman.</i>

140
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:57,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

141
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:21,700
[CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

142
00:08:26,267 --> 00:08:27,733
[CLUB MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:08:27,867 --> 00:08:29,967
- Sir, I'll just use the toilet.
<i> - Okay.</i>

144
00:08:31,967 --> 00:08:33,233
<i> Thank you.</i>

145
00:08:33,367 --> 00:08:40,233
[CLUB MUSIC CONTINUES]

146
00:08:45,467 --> 00:08:47,067
<i> Hi, boss!</i>

147
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,933
<i> You're so pretty, my love!</i>

148
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:52,433
[BELINDA] Just tonight?

149
00:08:52,567 --> 00:08:55,167
<i>Not just tonight.
You're always pretty.</i>

150
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:59,067
<i>I knew you were coming,
so I dolled up.</i>

151
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:06,967
[YOUNG RUDY]<i> I promised
</i> that when I get the gold,

152
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:09,367
<i> I'd come back for Belinda</i>

153
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:12,067
<i>and help her
get out of this rut.</i>

154
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,500
<i>I vowed to give her
a better life</i>

155
00:09:14,633 --> 00:09:17,967
<i>and devote all my love
to her.</i>

156
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,900
<i>Rudy, how many weeks
do you think it will take?</i>

157
00:09:21,033 --> 00:09:23,100
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> Looking at the map, sir,</i>

158
00:09:23,233 --> 00:09:26,333
<i>there are a lot of tunnels
and passages.</i>

159
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:27,767
- [PICKAXES, SHOVELS THUNKING]
- [MINERS GRUNTING]

160
00:09:27,933 --> 00:09:30,300
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> Watch your head, sir. Careful.</i>

161
00:09:31,333 --> 00:09:33,700
[YOUNG MARIANO]
<i> Hey! Don't slack off!</i>

162
00:09:33,833 --> 00:09:35,433
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> Give me...</i>

163
00:09:35,567 --> 00:09:37,500
Give me six to ten months, sir.

164
00:09:39,033 --> 00:09:40,000
<i> Careful, sir.</i>

165
00:09:40,133 --> 00:09:44,000
[PICKAXES, SHOVELS THUNKING]

166
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:45,900
<i>- Sir.
- Rudy.</i>

167
00:09:46,033 --> 00:09:47,600
[YOUNG MARIANO]
<i> Sir, give them a deadline.</i>

168
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:50,700
<i>They might just be stalling
so you'd keep them employed.</i>

169
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:52,000
<i> That's not true, sir.</i>

170
00:09:52,867 --> 00:09:54,800
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> I also want to find the gold.</i>

171
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:57,333
<i>I can't wait to find it
to finally turn my life around.</i>

172
00:09:57,467 --> 00:10:00,300
[YOUNG RICARDO]
<i> Me, too. I can't wait.</i>

173
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:04,233
<i>Because I've got so many plans
for that treasure.</i>

174
00:10:04,400 --> 00:10:05,867
[YOUNG RICARDO SIGHS]

175
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:12,267
[PICKAXES, SHOVELS THUNKING]

176
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:17,033
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> We dug for several weeks.</i>

177
00:10:18,567 --> 00:10:21,067
<i> We kept looking for gold.</i>

178
00:10:21,967 --> 00:10:24,933
<i>- Dude!
- This is hopeless! I quit!</i>

179
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,067
[MINER GRUNTS]

180
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:30,033
<i>My fellow miners
slowly lost hope.</i>

181
00:10:30,667 --> 00:10:32,233
<i> But I didn't stop.</i>

182
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:38,133
<i>Because I believed
that I will find the gold</i>

183
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,800
<i> that will change my life.</i>

184
00:10:40,933 --> 00:10:42,600
<i>I don't think
we'll find it here.</i>

185
00:10:42,733 --> 00:10:45,100
<i>- But the map says it's here.
- There's nothing here.</i>

186
00:10:45,233 --> 00:10:47,367
<i>- Rudy!
- Bring him to the base!</i>

187
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:48,400
[YOUNG MARIANO] Rudy!

188
00:10:48,533 --> 00:10:49,567
[YOUNG RICARDO] Well?!

189
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,600
<i>- Sir.
- We've been digging for weeks</i>

190
00:10:51,733 --> 00:10:53,100
<i> and still nothing!</i>

191
00:10:53,233 --> 00:10:55,067
<i> We're slowly losing our men!</i>

192
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:57,967
<i>Sir, the map says
it's here somewhere.</i>

193
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,700
<i>Do you really know
how to read a map?</i>

194
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:02,067
<i>Perhaps that map's fake
and you're just deceiving us.</i>

195
00:11:03,233 --> 00:11:04,700
<i> Sir, I am not deceiving you.</i>

196
00:11:04,833 --> 00:11:06,367
<i>I can feel it. We're so close
to finding that treasure!</i>

197
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:09,367
<i>But it looks like we're just
wasting our time and money here.</i>

198
00:11:09,533 --> 00:11:10,500
<i> Let's just go home.</i>

199
00:11:10,633 --> 00:11:12,100
<i> It's not worth the effort!</i>

200
00:11:12,233 --> 00:11:13,500
<i>Are we really going
to give up now, sir?</i>

201
00:11:13,633 --> 00:11:16,600
<i>Now, when we're so close
to finding the treasure?</i>

202
00:11:16,733 --> 00:11:17,800
<i> That's the problem with you.</i>

203
00:11:17,933 --> 00:11:20,733
<i>You keep saying
we're so close to finding gold,</i>

204
00:11:20,867 --> 00:11:21,800
<i> but where is it?!</i>

205
00:11:21,933 --> 00:11:23,333
<i> I'm bleeding money, Rudy!</i>

206
00:11:24,067 --> 00:11:25,767
Sir, just give me one more day.

207
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:26,933
<i> Please, sir.</i>

208
00:11:27,067 --> 00:11:28,933
<i>We've almost scoured
the whole cave, sir.</i>

209
00:11:29,067 --> 00:11:30,900
<i>You've lost your mind!
Let's go home!</i>

210
00:11:31,033 --> 00:11:32,433
<i>- Come on.
- Sir!</i>

211
00:11:32,567 --> 00:11:36,233
<i>Sir, if you stop looking now,
you're going to regret it.</i>

212
00:11:36,367 --> 00:11:39,267
<i>I'm already
regretting this, Rudy.</i>

213
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,433
<i> I shouldn't have believed you!</i>

214
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,167
<i> I thought you were bold.</i>

215
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,867
<i>It turns out you're
too afraid to gamble.</i>

216
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,633
<i>You're giving up
too easily.</i>

217
00:11:47,767 --> 00:11:49,233
<i> You think I'm giving up?</i>

218
00:11:49,367 --> 00:11:50,400
<i> You're a coward!</i>

219
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:52,500
- [BLOW LANDS]
<i> - Don't interfere!</i>

220
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:57,767
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

221
00:11:58,767 --> 00:12:00,367
[BLOWS LANDING]

222
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:02,633
[SHOVEL RATTLING]

223
00:12:02,767 --> 00:12:03,867
[THWACKS]

224
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,300
[BODY THUDDING]

225
00:12:06,433 --> 00:12:07,967
[SHOVEL CLATTERS]

226
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,400
[GUN COCKS]

227
00:12:13,467 --> 00:12:16,967
<i> I can bury you alive here.</i>

228
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:23,800
<i>You don't know
who you're messing with.</i>

229
00:12:23,933 --> 00:12:30,800
[ANGSTY MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,333
<i> Come on, let's go.</i>

231
00:12:39,467 --> 00:12:41,867
<i>Boss said it's time
to head home. Let's go!</i>

232
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,333
<i>- Let's go.
- Come on.</i>

233
00:12:48,367 --> 00:12:53,667
[SHOVEL SCRAPING DIRT]

234
00:12:53,800 --> 00:13:00,467
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING,
THEN FADES]

235
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:06,967
<i> I'm doing this for you.</i>

236
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,633
<i> I don't know if I messed up</i>

237
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,867
<i> or if I'm just unlucky.</i>

238
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,533
[RUDY]
Even I'm losing hope.

239
00:13:25,033 --> 00:13:27,367
Whatever I end up finding...

240
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:28,767
[GRUNTING]

241
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:35,500
It was the only way
I could win Belinda over.

242
00:13:35,633 --> 00:13:37,900
[SHOVEL SCRAPING DIRT]

243
00:13:38,033 --> 00:13:44,967
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

244
00:13:46,733 --> 00:13:51,900
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

245
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:56,467
<i>Should I go through with it
or back out now?</i>

246
00:13:56,633 --> 00:14:03,500
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:14:06,867 --> 00:14:11,000
[COIN CHIMES]

248
00:14:11,133 --> 00:14:14,100
[COIN THUDDING]

249
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:17,000
<i> Hey...</i>

250
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:19,733
<i> Where did you go?!</i>

251
00:14:19,867 --> 00:14:25,433
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

252
00:14:25,567 --> 00:14:26,900
<i> Hey, where are you?!</i>

253
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:32,633
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

254
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,933
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

255
00:14:36,067 --> 00:14:38,067
<i> I thought you were leaving me.</i>

256
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:49,533
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

257
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:10,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:15:12,633 --> 00:15:15,167
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

259
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,867
[HASP RATTLES]

260
00:15:21,533 --> 00:15:23,067
[HAMMERING CHEST]

261
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:30,067
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

262
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,700
[METAL CLANGING, THUDS]

263
00:15:35,867 --> 00:15:40,533
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

264
00:15:40,667 --> 00:15:45,500
[WONDROUS MUSIC PLAYING]

265
00:15:45,633 --> 00:15:47,600
[RUDY]
When I saw the gold,

266
00:15:48,867 --> 00:15:50,467
I got blinded by greed.

267
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:54,533
I forgot all my promises
to Ricardo.

268
00:15:54,667 --> 00:16:01,133
My only thought was, "I'm going
to get rich and win your mom."

269
00:16:03,433 --> 00:16:04,800
<i> Whoo!</i>

270
00:16:04,933 --> 00:16:11,700
[WONDROUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:16:11,867 --> 00:16:16,133
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

272
00:16:18,133 --> 00:16:24,533
[SENSUAL MUSIC PLAYING]

273
00:16:25,467 --> 00:16:27,533
[RUDY]<i> When I got
</i> the treasure...

274
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:31,233
<i> I went back for Belinda.</i>

275
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:33,833
- Sir, you're so handsome!
- You're handsome!

276
00:16:33,967 --> 00:16:36,800
- Come inside, sir!
- Come in!

277
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,033
- [BOUNCER] Sir, good evening.
- Good evening.

278
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:43,900
[RUDY]<i> If there was
</i> anything greater

279
00:16:44,033 --> 00:16:45,400
<i> than the treasure I got...</i>

280
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:48,167
<i> It's your mom.</i>

281
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:53,967
<i>I did everything
to make her fall for me.</i>

282
00:16:56,500 --> 00:17:03,400
[SENSUAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:22,000
[SENSUAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

284
00:17:22,133 --> 00:17:24,200
- Hey.
- [STAFF] Yes, sir?

285
00:17:27,767 --> 00:17:29,900
- Bring her to my table.
- Yes, sir!

286
00:17:37,433 --> 00:17:39,000
[BELINDA] Ma? You called for me?

287
00:17:39,133 --> 00:17:41,933
[WOMAN] Yeah.
That man asked for you.

288
00:17:42,067 --> 00:17:44,833
- He looks rich! Come! Yeah!
- Rich? Really?

289
00:17:44,967 --> 00:17:46,433
Sir!

290
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:49,733
Belinda is here.

291
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:54,967
Well, I'll take my leave.

292
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,633
Sit down.

293
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,233
You're probably cold.

294
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,167
Huh?

295
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,967
- This is a first.
- What?

296
00:18:14,567 --> 00:18:15,767
This.

297
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:17,167
[BELINDA CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

298
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:22,500
Usually, the men who ask for me
want me almost naked.

299
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:24,567
Well, I'm different from them.

300
00:18:26,533 --> 00:18:27,900
[BELINDA CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

301
00:18:28,033 --> 00:18:29,367
Mm.

302
00:18:29,933 --> 00:18:30,967
It's hot.

303
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,700
Mm.

304
00:18:33,733 --> 00:18:36,667
- Mm.
- Eat slowly. You might choke.

305
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:38,600
- Drink first.
- I'm sorry.

306
00:18:41,033 --> 00:18:42,000
Wait.

307
00:18:43,233 --> 00:18:45,167
I've never seen you here before.

308
00:18:45,733 --> 00:18:47,000
I'm from the province.

309
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:51,500
Where's your province?
I came from the province, too!

310
00:18:52,133 --> 00:18:54,100
But I haven't been home
for a long time

311
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:56,567
'cause the fare's too expensive.
[SIGHS]

312
00:18:56,733 --> 00:19:00,633
Instead of going there,

313
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:03,533
I just send the money
to my mom.

314
00:19:03,667 --> 00:19:05,400
It's more important
that she buys her medicine

315
00:19:05,533 --> 00:19:06,700
than see me.

316
00:19:09,167 --> 00:19:10,733
I'm sorry.
Am I talking too much?

317
00:19:10,867 --> 00:19:12,833
No, that's fine. That's fine.

318
00:19:15,867 --> 00:19:17,000
Your watch is beautiful.

319
00:19:18,333 --> 00:19:19,400
What's your job?

320
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:21,633
Nothing.

321
00:19:22,433 --> 00:19:24,000
I'm just an heir.

322
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:28,233
An heir? Wow! Then you have
no money problems.

323
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,433
[BELINDA SIGHS DEEPLY]

324
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,567
That's why when you live
with me,

325
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,667
you won't worry
about money anymore.

326
00:19:35,067 --> 00:19:40,967
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:42,367
I'm serious.

328
00:19:43,867 --> 00:19:45,367
I can change your life.

329
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,267
You don't have
to work here anymore.

330
00:19:48,267 --> 00:19:49,767
I'll change your world.

331
00:19:51,767 --> 00:19:54,167
- What's your name?
- Rudy.

332
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:56,633
Rudy Magtibay.

333
00:19:56,767 --> 00:19:58,267
[BELINDA CHUCKLING]

334
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:01,167
Your last name doesn't sound
like that of an heir's.

335
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:02,267
[BELINDA CHUCKLES]

336
00:20:02,433 --> 00:20:04,800
You have to get used
to the name Magtibay.

337
00:20:04,933 --> 00:20:05,867
Why?

338
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Because it'll soon be
your last name.

339
00:20:08,133 --> 00:20:09,100
Really?

340
00:20:10,033 --> 00:20:11,067
Belinda...

341
00:20:12,233 --> 00:20:13,200
...Magtibay.

342
00:20:14,233 --> 00:20:21,200
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:43,233
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

344
00:20:50,267 --> 00:20:51,533
[BELINDA EXHALES]

345
00:20:54,367 --> 00:20:55,333
Why?

346
00:20:56,467 --> 00:20:58,233
I can do this
for the rest of my life.

347
00:21:01,333 --> 00:21:02,233
What?

348
00:21:03,233 --> 00:21:04,433
Looking at you.

349
00:21:05,567 --> 00:21:06,833
Just staring at you.

350
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,567
[BELINDA BREATHES]

351
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:11,167
- Ah.
- Hm?

352
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:12,467
- Let me.
- Hm.

353
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:20,333
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:21,967
Let's get married.

355
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:23,167
[BELINDA COUGHS]

356
00:21:24,267 --> 00:21:27,067
What's with you?
Don't joke like that.

357
00:21:27,900 --> 00:21:30,567
I might just start
believing you.

358
00:21:31,233 --> 00:21:32,467
And then I'll start hoping.

359
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,467
Why won't you take me seriously?

360
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:37,433
Belinda, I want to be with you
for the rest of my life.

361
00:21:38,700 --> 00:21:40,267
[BELINDA BREATHES DEEPLY]

362
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,267
We just got to know each other.

363
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:46,500
There are things in our lives
that only happen once.

364
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:50,500
We shouldn't let them
just slip away.

365
00:21:51,867 --> 00:21:53,233
Why me?

366
00:21:55,733 --> 00:21:56,800
From the moment I saw you,

367
00:21:56,933 --> 00:21:59,700
I knew I wanted to spend
my life with you, Belinda.

368
00:22:00,333 --> 00:22:02,067
You don't know
what I went through

369
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,467
just to have
this chance, Belinda.

370
00:22:05,367 --> 00:22:08,400
We'll run away.
We'll forget about...

371
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:10,600
...the bad things that happened
in our past.

372
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:12,900
We'll change our lives, Belinda.

373
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:14,600
We'll have a family.

374
00:22:16,433 --> 00:22:18,800
One that's happy and complete.

375
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:26,800
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

376
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:31,400
Are you ready to be...

377
00:22:32,567 --> 00:22:34,133
...Mrs. Belinda Magtibay?

378
00:22:35,767 --> 00:22:42,733
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

379
00:22:57,800 --> 00:23:04,733
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:23:13,467 --> 00:23:15,467
<i>- Are we there yet?
- Yes, we're here.</i>

381
00:23:16,267 --> 00:23:18,200
Carding, open the gate, please!

382
00:23:18,333 --> 00:23:21,033
<i>- Who's Carding?
- Sir Rudy, good morning.</i>

383
00:23:21,167 --> 00:23:23,033
<i> Can I look now?</i>

384
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:25,733
<i>- Just take one more step.
- Okay.</i>

385
00:23:25,867 --> 00:23:28,333
<i>- There. Yes.
- Can I look now?</i>

386
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:32,333
<i> Wow! That's a huge house.</i>

387
00:23:32,467 --> 00:23:33,733
<i> Whose house is it?</i>

388
00:23:33,867 --> 00:23:36,333
<i>- It's ours.
- It's ours?!</i>

389
00:23:36,467 --> 00:23:38,067
<i> Really?</i>

390
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:42,767
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:43,833
[DOOR OPENS]

392
00:23:43,967 --> 00:23:50,933
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

393
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:02,500
- [YOUNG RUDY CHUCKLES]
- [BELINDA SQUEALS]

394
00:24:02,633 --> 00:24:04,367
[BELINDA]<i> Is this for real?
</i> This is ours?

395
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:05,767
- [BELINDA]<i> It's ours?
</i>- [YOUNG RUDY] Yes.

396
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:08,500
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> All of this is ours!</i>

397
00:24:11,833 --> 00:24:13,767
[BELINDA]<i> I'm so lucky
</i> to have you.

398
00:24:13,900 --> 00:24:16,867
<i> And so does our child.</i>

399
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,267
<i>He's lucky to have you
as his father.</i>

400
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:26,200
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

401
00:24:26,333 --> 00:24:27,467
[YOUNG RUDY]
<i> We're almost there.</i>

402
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:30,267
[BELINDA GRUNTING]

403
00:24:30,433 --> 00:24:32,500
[MIDWIFE] I can see the baby.

404
00:24:32,633 --> 00:24:35,500
[BELINDA GRUNTING]

405
00:24:35,633 --> 00:24:42,533
- [BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [BABY CRYING]

406
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:46,233
[RUDY] You, Gabriel...

407
00:24:47,067 --> 00:24:51,500
are the most important blessing
<i> your mom and I received.</i>

408
00:24:52,833 --> 00:24:56,400
<i> Hi-yah! Hi-yah! Hi-yah!</i>

409
00:24:56,533 --> 00:24:59,500
[RUDY]<i> You brought happiness
</i> to our home.

410
00:25:00,633 --> 00:25:02,100
<i> That time...</i>

411
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:06,133
<i>there was nothing
I could want more.</i>

412
00:25:07,967 --> 00:25:11,333
<i> You and your mom...</i>

413
00:25:12,767 --> 00:25:15,567
<i> are my real treasure.</i>

414
00:25:20,467 --> 00:25:22,533
<i> Rudy! Come out here!</i>

415
00:25:22,667 --> 00:25:24,467
<i>Ricardo and I were supposed
to split this between us,</i>

416
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:26,033
<i> but I took his share.</i>

417
00:25:26,167 --> 00:25:27,467
<i>- Run!
- Aah!</i>

418
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:28,833
<i>Love, you have to go now!
Hurry!</i>

419
00:25:28,967 --> 00:25:30,033
<i> Mommy loves you so much.</i>

420
00:25:30,167 --> 00:25:32,433
<i>No matter what happens,
always stay good, okay?</i>

421
00:25:32,567 --> 00:25:35,333
<i>Don't forget everything
I taught you.</i>

422
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:36,767
<i> Have mercy on my family.</i>

423
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:39,167
<i>Take me instead.
Spare my son and husband.</i>

424
00:25:39,300 --> 00:25:41,567
<i>- Mama!
- I need to find that cop.</i>

425
00:25:41,700 --> 00:25:43,900
<i>He has to pay
for what he did to my mother.</i>

426
00:25:44,033 --> 00:25:45,367
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [GROANS]

427
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:47,667
<i>Well, Samantha?!
Are you still alive?!</i>

428
00:25:47,800 --> 00:25:50,367
<i>Have you found the guy
I got into a fight with?</i>

429
00:25:50,900 --> 00:25:53,700
<i>He better hide
before I find him.</i>

430
00:25:57,300 --> 00:25:58,867
- [SCREAMING]
- [GUNSHOT]

431
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,667
<i>If you know you're right,
you should fight for it.</i>

432
00:26:01,800 --> 00:26:03,167
<i> Help!</i>

433
00:26:03,300 --> 00:26:04,400
<i> Aah!</i>

434
00:26:04,533 --> 00:26:10,200
- [GRUNTING]
- [BLOWS LANDING]

435
00:26:10,367 --> 00:26:11,700
<i> Help!</i>
